== Preservation and exact scope
The first two SDK binding builds fail before compilation because tracked
local dependencies are off disk. Existing dependency/metadata files are
materialized without changing their bytes; v3 builds against the actual
repository SDK. Errors and commands remain retained. One unused relation-
checker argument generates a retained warning; all gates and seals pass.

All gates use one build worker and the common reservation, with 8 GiB
address-space and a 1200-second aggregate envelope after queue admission.
Shared-host/build clocks are diagnostic. These different suites are not
comparable performance samples, so the diagram shows verification roles.

== Prospective full experiment
All 42 original phi/doubling arms remain fixed. Decode repetitions and
signed cancellation, then independently enumerate every four-ordinary-slot /
one-image public-point relation. Require exact weighted-set equality, the
old distinct subset, retained zero/projective rows, separate fraction-free
rank and full-rank public-point checks. Run first/audit/A/A/parity for all
cases; failed/missing positions remain explicit. Finite-Fp-seen and non-Fp-
seen sets can overlap: report their actual difference before claiming loss
from pruning. Independently check every q candidate by Horner evaluation.

The identity path checks all 21 public fixtures, actual modulus/model and
prime-order generator, derives the full order from its unique Hasse multiple,
and calls the native SDK. Both complete processes share one 1200-second
production envelope. Catalog parity, registry import, all 42 input bindings
and exact EC1/UID metadata parity remain required. Preserve frozen labels.

